\DOC SPECL_TAC

\TYPE {SPECL_TAC : term list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Generalises the goal's conclusion by universally quantifying over the given
list of variables, in the order supplied.

\DESCRIBE
The single argument is a {term list} of variables {x1 ... xn}, which become new
leading universal quantifiers on the goal's conclusion; the assumptions are
unchanged, the conclusion is otherwise untouched, and other free variables are
left free.
{
   A ?- t
   ========================  SPECL_TAC [x1; ...; xn]
   A ?- !x1 ... xn. t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this generalising behaviour appears, always on
goals with no assumptions and with argument lists of variables already
occurring free in the conclusion.

\ENDDOC
